{"id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave","title":"ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave","path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.md","line":756,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex#ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave","uses":["[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#def:shock-entropy-condition]]","[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:burgers-shock-formation]]","[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock]]","[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex","label":"ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave","line":1085,"source":"\\begin{example}[Shock and rarefaction combined for Burgers' equation]\n\\label{ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave}\n\\uses{def:shock-entropy-condition, ex:burgers-shock-formation, ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock, prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition}\n\\dcref{ch3:3.4-ex-3}\n\\group{Conservation Laws}\n\nFor $g=0$ on $x<0$, $g=1$ on $0\\le x\\le1$, and $g=0$ on $x>1$, the\nsolution for $0\\le t\\le2$ is\n\\[\nu=0\\ (x<0),\\quad u=x/t\\ (0<x<t),\\quad u=1\\ (t<x<1+t/2),\n\\quad u=0\\ (x>1+t/2).\n\\]\nFor $t\\ge2$ the shock curve obeys\n$\\dot s=s/(2t)$, $s(2)=2$, hence $s(t)=\\sqrt{2t}$, with $u=x/t$ to its\nleft and $u=0$ to its right.\n\\end{example}","html":" <p></p>\\begin{example} \\end{example}[Shock and rarefaction combined for Burgers&#x27; equation] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-65783a627572676572732d747269616e67756c61722d73686f636b2d77617665\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter3%23def%3Ashock-entropy-condition\">↗ def:shock-entropy-condition</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter3%23ex%3Aburgers-shock-formation\">↗ ex:burgers-shock-formation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter3%23ex%3Ararefaction-nonphysical-shock\">↗ ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter3%23prop%3Arankine-hugoniot-condition\">↗ prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.4-ex-3</span></span>\\group Conservation Laws <p></p>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g=0$\">$g=0$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x&lt;0$\">$x&lt;0$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g=1$\">$g=1$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\le x\\le 1$\">$0\\le x\\le 1$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g=0$\">$g=0$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x&gt;1$\">$x&gt;1$</span>, the solution for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\le t\\le 2$\">$0\\le t\\le 2$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  u=0\\  (x&lt;0),\\quad u=x/t\\  (0&lt;x&lt;t),\\quad u=1\\  (t&lt;x&lt;1+t/2), \\quad u=0\\  (x&gt;1+t/2).  \\]\">\\[  u=0\\  (x&lt;0),\\quad u=x/t\\  (0&lt;x&lt;t),\\quad u=1\\  (t&lt;x&lt;1+t/2), \\quad u=0\\  (x&gt;1+t/2).  \\]</span> For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\ge 2$\">$t\\ge 2$</span> the shock curve obeys <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\dot s=s/(2t)$\">$\\dot s=s/(2t)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s(2)=2$\">$s(2)=2$</span>, hence <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s(t)=\\sqrt{2t}$\">$s(t)=\\sqrt{2t}$</span>, with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u=x/t$\">$u=x/t$</span> to its left and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u=0$\">$u=0$</span> to its right. \\end{example}","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: example、group"]},"previous":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#rem:entropy-condition-uniform-convexity","next":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#sec:lax-oleinik-formula","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#def:shock-entropy-condition","title":"def:shock-entropy-condition","label":"def:shock-entropy-condition"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:burgers-shock-formation","title":"ex:burgers-shock-formation","label":"ex:burgers-shock-formation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock","title":"ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock","label":"ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition","title":"prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition","label":"prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:burgers-example-n-wave-specialization","title":"ex:burgers-example-n-wave-specialization","label":"ex:burgers-example-n-wave-specialization"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave","title":"ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave","tex":"\\begin{example}[Shock and rarefaction combined for Burgers' equation]\n\\label{ex:burgers-triangular-shock-wave}\n\\uses{def:shock-entropy-condition, ex:burgers-shock-formation, ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock, prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition}\n\\dcref{ch3:3.4-ex-3}\n\\group{Conservation Laws}\n\nFor $g=0$ on $x<0$, $g=1$ on $0\\le x\\le1$, and $g=0$ on $x>1$, the\nsolution for $0\\le t\\le2$ is\n\\[\nu=0\\ (x<0),\\quad u=x/t\\ (0<x<t),\\quad u=1\\ (t<x<1+t/2),\n\\quad u=0\\ (x>1+t/2).\n\\]\nFor $t\\ge2$ the shock curve obeys\n$\\dot s=s/(2t)$, $s(2)=2$, hence $s(t)=\\sqrt{2t}$, with $u=x/t$ to its\nleft and $u=0$ to its right.\n\\end{example}","source":"tex/references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#def:shock-entropy-condition","title":"def:shock-entropy-condition","description":""},{"node":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:burgers-shock-formation","title":"ex:burgers-shock-formation","description":""},{"node":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock","title":"ex:rarefaction-nonphysical-shock","description":""},{"node":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition","title":"prop:rankine-hugoniot-condition","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}